    "interpretation": "The Eminton-Lord collocation matrix condition number grows ~n^3.1 (1.9e6 at n=200, 1.2e8 at n=800). The mesh-derived Mach-cut area distributions are not smooth (rms second difference 0.006-0.20 m^2, single-slice jumps up to 2.8 m^2), so refining the slice count injects more high-frequency discretization noise that the ill-conditioned solve amplifies: the area-rule D/q rises from 15.50 to 44.44 m^2 (2.87x) instead of converging. The large per-theta outliers (742 m^2 at theta=73.5 deg) are numerical artefacts of oblique cuts through a triangulated surface, not physical wave drag."
